      "visualLineId": null,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 62,
      "str": "The dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or",
      "x": 143.56,
      "y": 371.04,
      "width": 324.74,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 468.3,
      "visualLineId": 13,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 63,
      "str": "convolutional neural networks that include an encoder and a decoder. The best",
      "x": 143.87,
      "y": 360.13,
      "width": 324.26,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 468.13,
      "visualLineId": 14,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 64,
      "str": "performing models also connect the encoder and decoder through an attention",
      "x": 143.87,
      "y": 349.22,
      "width": 324.26,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 468.13,
      "visualLineId": 15,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 65,
      "str": "mechanism. We propose a new simple network architecture, the Transformer,",
      "x": 143.87,
      "y": 338.31,
      "width": 325.51,
      "height": 9.96,
      "right": 469.38,
      "visualLineId": 16,
      "inferredColumn": null
    },
    {
      "itemIndex": 66,
      "str": "based solely on attention mechanisms, dispensing with recurrence and convolutions",
